.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH SP2P-SERVER 1 "2025" "sp2p" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sp2p\-server \- signaling and relay server for sp2p
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sp2p\-server
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sp2p\-server
runs the signaling server that coordinates peer-to-peer connections for
.BR sp2p (1)
clients.
It serves the web UI, handles WebSocket signaling, and optionally provides
TURN relay and TLS termination.
.PP
The signaling service cannot decrypt content between trusted clients.
A compromised host serving browser JavaScript or bootstrap scripts can replace
client code; use independently trusted CLI installations for that threat model.
.PP
By default, shell and PowerShell bootstraps check archive SHA-256 against the same fixed
GitHub release's checksum manifest before extraction, without requiring GitHub
CLI. They trust the GitHub HTTPS release channel, not an independently verified
signer. Unavailable pinned releases and local development archives cannot
bootstrap; use a locally built CLI for development.
.PP
The explicit first bootstrap argument
.B \-\-insecure\-skip\-checksum
skips checksum-manifest and digest checks, with a warning to stderr.
It is consumed by the script and is not a server or installed CLI flag.
TLS certificate checks and release/platform URL validation remain enabled.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-addr " address"
Listen address.
Default:
.IR :8080 .
.TP
.BI \-base\-url " url"
Public base URL for generating share links and configuring CORS.
Default:
.IR http://localhost:8080 .
.TP
.BI \-config\-dir " dir"
Directory for persistent data such as ACME certificates.
Default:
.IR ~/.config/sp2p .
.SS TLS
.TP
.B \-acme
Enable automatic TLS certificates via ACME (Let's Encrypt).
The domain is derived from
.BR \-base\-url .
.TP
.BI \-acme\-email " email"
Contact email for ACME certificate registration.
.TP
.BI \-tls\-cert " file"
Path to a TLS certificate file (for manual TLS).
.TP
.BI \-tls\-key " file"
Path to the corresponding TLS private key file.
.SS TURN Relay
.TP
.BI \-turn\-servers " urls"
Comma-separated list of TURN server URLs
(e.g.
.IR turn:turn.example.com:3478 ).
.TP
.BI \-turn\-username " user"
Static TURN username.
.TP
.BI \-turn\-password " pass"
Static TURN password.
.TP
.BI \-turn\-secret " secret"
Shared secret for generating ephemeral TURN credentials.
Mutually exclusive with static username/password.
.TP
.BI \-turn\-ttl " duration"
TTL for ephemeral TURN credentials.
Must be positive and no greater than one hour. Both paired peers share one
cached issuance per session; repeated requests do not renew its lifetime.
New issuances are limited to 120 per minute globally and 12 per sender IP.
Anonymous relay use still requires external allocation/bandwidth quotas and
destination-address restrictions. Static credentials remain reusable.
Default:
.IR 5m .
.SS Reverse Proxy
.TP
.B \-trust\-proxy
Trust
.B X\-Forwarded\-For
headers only from explicitly trusted proxy addresses, for all client-IP limits.
Requires
.BR \-trusted\-proxies .
Environment values false and 0 disable trust.
.TP
.BI \-trusted\-proxies " addresses"
Comma-separated IP addresses/CIDRs of the actual reverse proxies.
Forwarded chains are resolved from the trusted side. Do not trust all addresses.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All flags can be set via environment variables:
.PP
.TS
l l.
Flag	Variable
\-addr	SP2P_ADDR
\-base\-url	SP2P_BASE_URL
\-config\-dir	SP2P_CONFIG_DIR
\-acme	SP2P_ACME
\-acme\-email	SP2P_ACME_EMAIL
\-tls\-cert	SP2P_TLS_CERT
\-tls\-key	SP2P_TLS_KEY
\-trust\-proxy	SP2P_TRUST_PROXY
\-trusted\-proxies	SP2P_TRUSTED_PROXIES
\-turn\-servers	SP2P_TURN_SERVERS
\-turn\-username	SP2P_TURN_USERNAME
\-turn\-password	SP2P_TURN_PASSWORD
\-turn\-secret	SP2P_TURN_SECRET
\-turn\-ttl	SP2P_TURN_TTL
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a local development server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p-server
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with automatic TLS on a public domain:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p-server \\
    -base-url https://sp2p.example.com \\
    -acme \\
    -acme-email admin@example.com \\
    -addr :443
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with manual TLS certificates:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p-server \\
    -base-url https://sp2p.example.com \\
    -tls-cert /etc/ssl/sp2p.crt \\
    -tls-key /etc/ssl/sp2p.key \\
    -addr :443
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run behind nginx with TURN relay:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p-server \\
    -base-url https://sp2p.example.com \\
    -trust-proxy \\
    -trusted-proxies 127.0.0.1/32,::1/128 \\
    -turn-servers turn:turn.example.com:3478 \\
    -turn-secret mysecret
.fi
.RE
.SH CONTAINERS AND UPGRADES
Clients and servers can be upgraded independently: signaling remains v2.
Two updated peers automatically use transfer v3, including through a 0.4.0
server; a transfer with a 0.4.0 peer automatically uses v2.
No version flag or browser checkbox is required.
Legacy transfers lack v3 candidate authentication and receive credits;
the server relays end-to-end capabilities without selecting a transfer version.
Both images run as UID/GID 65532 and use /config; persistent mounts must be
writable by that identity. Prefer TLS termination at a reverse proxy forwarding
to port 8080. Native low-port TLS/ACME requires explicit runtime low-port
permissions and routing, not a return to root. Validate renewal in staging.
.PP
Signaling sockets have a ten-second first-message deadline, bounded global
and per-IP admission, and per-socket traffic limits. Public TURN deployments
must configure and test the example coturn policy plus an egress firewall.
